    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461-a2">

                <pb facs="0553" n="469" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg469"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Lansdowne to Mr.
                            White.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-01-09"><hi rendition="#italic">January 9,
                        1903</hi>.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of to-day’s date, in which you are so good as to communicate to me,
                    in accordance with instructions from your Government, copy of a telegram
                    received yesterday by Mr. Secretary Hay from Mr. Bowen, United States minister
                    at Caracas, intimating that the Venezuelan Government accept the conditions
                    proposed by Great Britain and Germany, and suggesting that Mr. Bowen should at
                    once proceed to Washington to discuss the questions at issue with the
                    representatives of the powers at Washington.</p>
                <p>You add that Mr. Bowen will proceed to Washington immediately. This communication
                    will receive immediate attention.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansdowne.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
